# SSE fixtures are byte-exact captures of provider wire traffic, replayed by
# format-translation.test.ts. The SSE event separator is a blank line: the test
# harness splits on "\n\n". A CRLF fixture never matches it ("\r\n\r\n" contains
# no "\n\n"), so the whole capture arrives as one chunk, zero events parse, and
# the fixture-driven describes fail on an empty parse — indistinguishable from a
# real anthropic-sse regression. Measured on this branch 2026-10-26: converting
# the 32 fixtures to CRLF turns exactly 11 of 126 tests red (seed passthrough,
# 4 thinking-block filtering, 4 MiniMax M2.5, 2 in-stream #106); restoring LF
# returns them all green. `text` also normalizes CRLF back to LF when such a
# fixture is committed, so it cannot enter history in the first place.
# Keep them LF on every platform.
*.sse text eol=lf
